# Cursor Agent Ruleset: High-Performance GitHub Pages Portfolio

## 1. Project Architecture
- You are an expert Frontend Engineer building a static site for GitHub Pages.
- Structure: Gateway (index.html) -> /projects/ (index.html) and /photography/ (index.html).
- Tech: HTML5, Tailwind CSS, and Vanilla JS (No Node.js/Backend).

## 2. Asset Management & Performance
- All images must be stored in `/assets/images/` and categorized (e.g., /photography/, /ui/).
- Format: Always prioritize .webp for images.
- Relative Paths: Use relative paths (e.g., ../assets/...) to ensure compatibility with GitHub subdomains.
- Lazy Loading: Every <img> tag must include `loading="lazy"`.
- Layout Stability: Use aspect-ratio containers (Tailwind `aspect-square` or `aspect-video`) to prevent Layout Shift (CLS).

## 3. Directory Structure
Ensure the Agent adheres to this tree:
/root
├── index.html (Gateway)
├── projects/index.html
├── photography/index.html
├── assets/
│   ├── images/ (photography, projects, ui)
│   ├── css/
│   └── js/
└── .nojekyll (Must be present for GitHub Pages)

## 4. Design Language
- Minimalism: High-impact typography, ample whitespace.
- Photography: Use a 3-column responsive grid with a smooth hover-zoom effect: `transition-transform duration-500 hover:scale-105`.
- Interactivity: Ensure navigation between sections is seamless and fast.

## 5. Deployment Readiness
- Do not use server-side routing. Use folder-based routing for clean URLs.
- Reference the .github/workflows/deploy.yml for deployment logic.

## 6. Project Card Standards
- Layout: Use a responsive grid (1 col on mobile, 2 or 3 on desktop).
- Consistency: Project thumbnails must use `aspect-video` to match the photography gallery's precision.
- Interactivity: Cards should have a `hover:shadow-xl` and `hover:scale-[1.02]` effect to provide tactile feedback.
- Content: Every card must include a Title, Description, Tech Stack tags, and at least one Action Link.

## 7. Bio & Personality Rule
- Persona: A blend of technical rigor (Data Security) and creative passion (Photography).
- Tone: Empathetic, insightful, and slightly modern/minimalist.
- Localization: Subtly reference the Indonesian context (e.g., Karawang, tropical gardening) to add authenticity.
- Typography: Use a serif font for headers (like Playfair Display) and a clean sans-serif for body text to create a "Portfolio" feel.

## 8. Lightbox Interaction
- Trigger: Use the class `.lightbox-trigger` on image containers.
- Data Attribute: Use `data-full` to store the path to the high-res WebP image.
- Behavior: Ensure the background scroll is disabled when the lightbox is open using `overflow: hidden`.
- Close: Allow closing via the 'X' button or by clicking the backdrop.

## 9. JavaScript Performance & Logic
- Keep it Vanilla: Avoid jQuery or heavy libraries unless specified.
- State Management: Use data-attributes (e.g., data-category="landscapes") for filtering logic.
- Persistence: Use `localStorage` for theme preferences (Dark/Light mode).
- Clean Code: Encapsulate JS functions into a single `main.js` or within script tags at the bottom of the body to prevent render-blocking.

## 10. Dark Mode Styling Rules
- Primary Strategy: Use Tailwind's `dark:` variant.
- Backgrounds: Use `dark:bg-gray-900` for main surfaces and `dark:bg-gray-800` for cards.
- Text: Use `dark:text-gray-100` for headers and `dark:text-gray-400` for body text.
- Borders: Soften borders in dark mode using `dark:border-gray-700`.
- Performance: Ensure the theme check script runs as early as possible (ideally in the <head>) to prevent "Flash of Unstyled Content" (FOUC).   